      "source": [
        "The code block performed the following actions:\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  **`telco[\"TotalCharges\"] = pd.to_numeric(telco[\"TotalCharges\"], errors=\"coerce\")`**:\n",
        "    *   This line converts the `TotalCharges` column to a numeric data type.\n",
        "    *   The `errors=\"coerce\"` argument is crucial here. If any value in the `TotalCharges` column cannot be converted to a number (e.g., if it's an empty string or a non-numeric string), it will be replaced with `NaN` (Not a Number).\n",
        "\n",
        "2.  **`telco[\"TotalCharges\"].fillna(telco[\"TotalCharges\"].median(), inplace=True)`**:\n",
        "    *   After coercing non-numeric values to `NaN`, this line handles those missing values.\n",
        "    *   `telco[\"TotalCharges\"].median()` calculates the median value of the `TotalCharges` column.\n",
        "    *   `fillna()` then replaces all `NaN` values in `TotalCharges` with this calculated median.\n",
        "    *   `inplace=True` modifies the DataFrame directly without needing to reassign the column.\n",
        "\n",
        "3.  **`telco.drop(\"customerID\", axis=1, inplace=True)`**:\n",
        "    *   This line removes the `customerID` column from the DataFrame.\n",
        "    *   `axis=1` specifies that a column should be dropped (as opposed to a row).\n",
        "    *   `inplace=True` ensures the change is made directly to the `telco` DataFrame.\n",
        "    *   Customer ID is typically an identifier and not useful for model training directly.\n",
        "\n",
        "4.  **`telco.isnull().sum().head()`**:\n",
        "    *   This line checks for any remaining missing values in the DataFrame.\n",
        "    *   `telco.isnull()` returns a boolean DataFrame indicating where values are `NaN`.\n",
        "    *   `.sum()` counts the number of `True` values (i.e., `NaN`s) for each column.\n",
        "    *   `.head()` displays the first few rows of this resulting Series, showing the count of missing values for the initial columns to confirm the cleaning was successful."
      ]
    },
