      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "I built a Customer Segmentation and Retention Analytics system to help businesses identify valuable customers, predict customer churn, and design targeted retention strategies.\n",
        "\n",
        "The project combines customer segmentation using purchasing behavior and churn prediction using machine learning.\n",
        "\n",
        "Part 1: Churn Prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "For churn prediction, I used the Telco Customer Churn dataset which contains customer demographics, contract details, service usage, and billing information.\n",
        "\n",
        "I first cleaned the data by handling missing values, converting data types, and encoding categorical variables. Then I trained a Random Forest classifier to predict whether a customer would churn.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model achieved a ROC-AUC score of around 0.83, which indicates good discrimination between customers who are likely to leave and those who are not.\n",
        "\n",
        "I also analyzed feature importance and found that customer tenure, contract type, and monthly charges were among the strongest churn drivers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Part 2: Customer Segmentation\n",
        "\n",
        "For customer segmentation, I used the Online Retail dataset and performed RFM analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "RFM stands for:\n",
        "\n",
        "Recency: how recently a customer purchased\n",
        "Frequency: how often they purchase\n",
        "Monetary: how much they spend\n",
        "\n",
        "I calculated these metrics for every customer and standardized them before applying K-Means clustering.\n",
        "\n",
        "The clustering grouped customers into behavioral segments such as High Value Loyal customers, Frequent Buyers, At-Risk customers, and Low Engagement customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Business Impact\n",
        "\n",
        "The most useful output was identifying high-value customers who showed signs of disengagement.\n",
        "\n",
        "Instead of giving retention offers to everyone, businesses can focus their marketing budget on customers who contribute significant revenue but are at risk of leaving.\n",
        "\n",
        "This mirrors how subscription platforms, e-commerce companies, and SaaS businesses optimize customer retention and maximize customer lifetime value\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "whxBypGRvMuc"
      }
